From: h713 <h713@local>
Date: Mon, 1 Sep 2026 23:55:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] EXPERIMENT: bind KMS to the AFBD block for a video-plane test

The current series leaves display@5600000 disabled and dec@5600000 okay, so the
AFBD KMS driver is built but never binds and there is no DRM target on the panel.
That arrangement was chosen to give DECD the block; it also means every
video-plane result so far was obtained with the *U-Boot* logo on the other
channel, never a KMS-driven one.

Patch 0065 tried to make the KMS driver's own RGB channel interpret NV12 and
failed, but its registers were only part of the story: it never enabled the
source, never gave it a size, never set the chroma gain and never wrote the
plane-1 downstream selector. Those are known now. What is still unknown is
whether the video plane can be lit at all while the KMS driver owns the block --
whether its bind-time reset or its atomic commits stomp the plane.

Enable KMS and disable DECD so that question can be asked directly. With DECD
absent there is no frame submission, so the test drives the video plane by
register poke against a static NV12 frame placed in the adopted scanout carveout
with /dev/mem, which is reachable because that region is no-map.

OUT OF SERIES. This is the inverse of the out-of-series 0068 and cannot be
applied with it: KMS and DECD share AFBD MMIO and SPI 110, so exactly one may
be enabled.

Signed-off-by: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy200-qz713df-a1.dts
@@ -48,3 +48,15 @@
 &motor_ctr { status = "disabled"; };
 &adc_keys { status = "disabled"; };
 &board_mgr { status = "disabled"; };
+
+/*
+ * Inverse of 0068: give the AFBD block to KMS so the video plane can be tested
+ * underneath a KMS-driven RGB channel rather than U-Boot's adopted logo.
+ */
+&display {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&dec {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
